{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 536963, "name": "Robert McLachlan", "username": "penguinista", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-10-11T04:53:14.952Z", "cooked": "<p>Is there a command that would get rid of files that are not connected to anything?<br>\nSorry if this sounds stupid I\"m just trying to clean up my Linux rig. Thanks for your help.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-10-11T18:21:13.084Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 33, "reads": 41, "readers_count": 40, "score": 178.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204325, "topic_slug": "safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies", "display_username": "Robert McLachlan", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 3, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34959, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies/204325/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 536965, "name": "Gregory Lee Bartholomew", "username": "glb", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/glb/{size}/570_2.png", "created_at": "2026-10-11T05:03:54.213Z", "cooked": "<p>“connected” is a tricky word to interpret. Just because a file is not owned by a package (according to the package database) does not mean that it is not important.</p>\n<p>That said, yes, you can query what package a file belongs to. The command is <code>rpm -qf &lt;path-to-file&gt;</code> (e.g. <code>rpm -qf /etc/hosts</code>). You would have to script that to find all the “unowned” files under a given directory.</p>\n<p>Beware that “getting rid of unowned files” is very much a “<a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoot_oneself_in_the_foot#English\">shoot yourself in the foot</a>” sort of operation and Linux <em>will</em> let you do that. <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=15\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>All that said, I have personally done such things in the past. I preferred to do it just before I did a major upgrade from one version of Fedora Linux to the next, on the theory that if I deleted some file that shouldn’t have been deleted, there would be at least a chance that it would be restored on the subsequent upgrade since that typically re-downloads and rewrites all the package files.</p>\n<p>Good luck and don’t forget to make backups. <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=15\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-10-11T05:06:02.152Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 41, "readers_count": 40, "score": 58.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204325, "topic_slug": "safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies", "display_username": "Gregory Lee Bartholomew", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoot_oneself_in_the_foot#English", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "shoot oneself in the foot - Wiktionary, the free dictionary", "clicks": 1}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 3}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 586, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "user_status": {"description": "chill'n", "emoji": "coffee", "ends_at": null, "message_bus_last_id": 1}, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies/204325/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 3}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 3, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 536968, "name": "Robert McLachlan", "username": "penguinista", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-10-11T05:10:35.655Z", "cooked": "<p>Thank you I’ll heed the warning!</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-10-11T05:10:35.655Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 39, "readers_count": 38, "score": 12.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204325, "topic_slug": "safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies", "display_username": "Robert McLachlan", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 586, "username": "glb", "name": "Gregory Lee Bartholomew", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/glb/{size}/570_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34959, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies/204325/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 537020, "name": "anon94964583", "username": "anon94964583", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/603e79/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-10-11T13:18:45.435Z", "cooked": "<p>Not sure if this will satisfy your needs but,<br>\neverytime you update the rpm’s are cached up so you can re install them quickly if needed you can clear it by</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf clean all\n</code></pre>\n<p>It dosent affect current programs, just frees up disk space.</p>\n<p>Give a read to<br>\n<iframe class=\"reddit-onebox\" src=\"https://embed.reddit.com/r/Fedora/comments/1cbmofj/how_safe_is_sudo_dnf_autoremove/?embed=true&amp;ref_source=embed&amp;ref=share\" width=\"640\" height=\"500\" allowfullscreen=\"\" seamless=\"seamless\" sandbox=\"allow-same-origin allow-scripts allow-forms allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox allow-presentation\"></iframe>\n<br>\nand</p><aside class=\"quote quote-modified\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"96885\">\n  <div class=\"title\">\n    <div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n    <img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/294172/48.png\" class=\"avatar\">\n    <div class=\"quote-title__text-content\">\n      <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/running-dnf-autoremove-should-i-be-removing-these-packages/96885\">Running dnf autoremove, should I be removing these packages?</a> <a class=\"badge-category__wrapper \" href=\"/c/ask/6\"><span data-category-id=\"6\" style=\"--category-badge-color: #38BC3B; --category-badge-text-color: #FFFFFF;\" data-drop-close=\"true\" class=\"badge-category --style-square \"><span class=\"badge-category__name\">Ask Fedora</span></span></a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <blockquote>\n    Hi, \nI just ran dnf autoremove to see if there are unneeded dependencies on my system which could be removed. This is the output: \n$ sudo dnf autoremove\nPackage                                Arch       Version                                Repository                Size\nRemoving:                                                                                                              \n amd-ucode-firmware                    noarch     20231111-1.fc39                        updates           …\n  </blockquote>\n</aside>\n\n<p>If you have a question let us know <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/smiley.png?v=15\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-10-11T13:20:31.309Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 31, "readers_count": 30, "score": 21.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204325, "topic_slug": "safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies", "display_username": "anon94964583", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/running-dnf-autoremove-should-i-be-removing-these-packages/96885", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Running dnf autoremove, should I be removing these packages?", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34189, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies/204325/4", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 537070, "name": "Robert McLachlan", "username": "penguinista", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-10-11T16:21:34.411Z", "cooked": "<p>Thank you</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-10-11T16:21:34.411Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 28, "readers_count": 27, "score": 25.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204325, "topic_slug": "safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies", "display_username": "Robert McLachlan", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 34959, "username": "penguinista", "name": "Robert McLachlan", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/294172/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34959, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies/204325/5", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 537120, "name": "Lars", "username": "l-c-g", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/l-c-g/{size}/36557_2.png", "created_at": "2026-10-11T18:24:03.190Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"penguinista\" data-display-name=\"Robert McLachlan\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"204325\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/294172/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Robert McLachlan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is there a command that would get rid of files that are not connected to anything?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That question is different from the title “Safely remove unused packages/dependencies”. For unused packages, you can run <code>sudo dnf autoremove</code>. It will remove any package that is marked as automatically installed but no longer has another package depend on it.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-10-11T18:24:03.190Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 39.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204325, "topic_slug": "safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies", "display_username": "Lars", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 20111, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies/204325/7", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}, {"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 537129, "name": "Joe Walker", "username": "grumpey", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png", "created_at": "2026-10-11T18:52:11.328Z", "cooked": "<p>You can double check what’s going to be removed with:<br>\n<code>dnf repoquery --unneeded </code></p>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-10-11T18:52:11.328Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 7, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 21, "readers_count": 20, "score": 29.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 204325, "topic_slug": "safely-remove-unused-packages-dependencies", "display_username": "Joe Walker", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_r